<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01295#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed to target individuals who hold negative views or prejudices against religious clergy and transgender people, particularly those who may be influenced by or propagate harmful stereotypes. The intended audience likely includes people who are familiar with or sensitive to religious institutions (specifically Catholic clergy, given the attire) and/or those who are opposed to or fearful of transgender identities. The meme's use of false equivalence and hate speech aims to provoke outrage and reinforce existing biases, making it particularly effective in communities that already harbor animosity toward these groups. The visual of the isolated clergyman and the text's accusatory tone are designed to resonate with audiences who are predisposed to fear or distrust religious figures and/or transgender individuals."@en .
