<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#AnalogicalMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Analogical Mapping is a mapping between one entity and another in the meme, usually between a visual element and a textual element. It follows the pattern: 'X is Y'. E.g. the juxtaposition of a certain text to some visual material creates a mapping between the text and the visual material."@en .
_:n06cbaefab1b841fda34e595d4e11518eb58 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:n06cbaefab1b841fda34e595d4e11518eb59 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01295#clergy> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractedFrom> "01295.png" .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01295#transgender> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The term 'transgender' refers to people whose gender identity differs from the sex they were assigned at birth. The meme uses this term in a derogatory and misleading way, attempting to equate transgender people with clergy by suggesting that 'clergy' is the correct term to describe men wearing dresses and molesting children. This is a false equivalence and contributes to transphobic sentiment."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#consilientWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "amplifies"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semanticallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatesTo> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundPreservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text placed only over neutral areas to preserve important visual content in memes"@en .
