_:n06cbaefab1b841fda34e595d4e11518eb14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01295#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The top text explicitly accuses 'men wearing dresses' (a gendered presentation) of molesting children. The visual of the clergyman, dressed in a red robe and white zucchetto (a gendered presentation of clerical attire), is presented as the target of this accusation. The meme uses the visual of the clergyman to represent the 'men wearing dresses' in the text, creating an analogical mapping where the clergyman is equated with the accused group. This mapping is reinforced by the text's implication that the clergyman is the one being referred to, even though the text is phrased as a question. The mapping is further supported by the visual of the solitary clergyman, which amplifies the stereotype being projected onto him."@en .
